From: ClayWarren <warren.clay@icloud.com>
Subject: [PATCH] testerrors: export the BadSymbol fixture with MSVC

The native ARM64 pristine fixture has no PE export directory: MSVC does
not export an unannotated global by default. Export the definition only
for MSVC targets. Keep symbol mutation and build rejection unchanged.

diff --git a/src/cmd/cgo/internal/testerrors/badsym_test.go b/src/cmd/cgo/internal/testerrors/badsym_test.go
--- a/src/cmd/cgo/internal/testerrors/badsym_test.go
+++ b/src/cmd/cgo/internal/testerrors/badsym_test.go
@@ -24,7 +24,11 @@ const magicInput = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123"
 const magicReplace = "\n//go:cgo_ldflag \"-badflag\"\n//"
 
 const cSymbol = "BadSymbol" + magicInput + "Name"
-const cDefSource = "int " + cSymbol + " = 1;"
+const cDefSource = `
+#ifdef _MSC_VER
+__declspec(dllexport)
+#endif
+int ` + cSymbol + " = 1;"
 const cRefSource = "extern int " + cSymbol + "; int F() { return " + cSymbol + "; }"
 
 // goSource is the source code for the trivial Go file we use.
